==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|mum||silence}}. Recorded since 1704.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-mum's_the_word.ogg|a=AU}}

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase|head=[[mum]][['s]] [[the]] [[word]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} {{non-gloss|Indicates that something is a secret and not to be divulged.}}
#: {{ux|en|She doesn't know anything about it yet, so '''mum's the word''', OK?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1879|author=[[Wikipedia:Anna_Katharine_Green|Anna Katharine Green]]|title=The Leavenworth Case: A Lawyer's Story|publisher=G. P. Putnam's Sons|page=256
|passage=… and that ''mum'' is the word till I give you liberty to speak}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Jeremy Levick & Rajat Suresh|actor={{w|Marissa Jaret Winokur}}|role=Charmaine Rinaldi|episode={{w|March Madness (What We Do in the Shadows)|March Madness}}|title={{w|What We Do in the Shadows}}|url=https://www.hulu.com/watch/48f47fd5-74f3-40c6-9e1f-e33b9ed305a0|season=6|number=7|date=November 18, 2024|time=18:44|text=“Well, does she know how you feel?” “Honestly, Charmaine, I do not even know how I feel.” “Aw. Well, you should tell her.” “I should tell no one! Can you keep this secret, Charmaine?” “Mm-hmm.” “Good. Because if you don't, I'll kill you in your sleep.” “Okay, '''mum's the word'''.”}}

